moon_excalidraw is written in MoonBit. It follows the behaviour of the projects
below, translating their algorithms, constants and the order of their
calculations, because its output has to match theirs byte for byte. None of
their source files are copied; their notices are reproduced here as their
licenses require.

  * excalidraw 0.18.1            https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw        MIT
      element model, how each element becomes rough.js calls, arrowheads,
      text layout, frames, and the SVG export
  * perfect-freehand 1.2.0       https://github.com/steveruizok/perfect-freehand MIT
      the outline of a hand-drawn stroke (src/freehand)
  * @braintree/sanitize-url 6.0.2 https://github.com/braintree/sanitize-url       MIT
      the cleaning of link targets (src/model/link.mbt)
  * V8 13.6 (src/base/ieee754.cc) https://github.com/v8/v8                        BSD-3-Clause
      the fdlibm routines behind Math.atan2 and Math.hypot (src/internal/jsnum)
  * roughjs 4.6.4                https://github.com/rough-stuff/rough            MIT
      used through the moon_rough package, which ports it; see
      https://github.com/sayoi7799/moon_rough

The test fixtures are SVG documents and JSON data produced by running the
packages above, and the files under fixtures/scenes were drawn with the
Excalidraw web app. They are distributed under the same terms as the project.

